    "problem_statement": "SVG image generation fails with UnboundLocalError\n\n#### Description\n\nWhen generating QR codes using any of the SVG image factories, the code crashes with an `UnboundLocalError` for the variable `units`. This affects all SVG-related functionality.\n\n#### Steps/Code to Reproduce\n\n```python\nimport qrcode\nfrom qrcode.image import svg\nimport io\n\n# This will fail\nqr = qrcode.QRCode()\nqr.add_data(\"test data\")\nimg = qr.make_image(image_factory=svg.SvgImage)\nimg.save(io.BytesIO())\n```\n\nThe same error occurs with other SVG factories:\n\n```python\n# These also fail\nimg = qr.make_image(image_factory=svg.SvgPathImage)\nimg = qr.make_image(image_factory=svg.SvgFragmentImage)\n```\n\n#### Expected Result\nSVG images should be generated successfully without errors.\n\n#### Actual Result\n```\nUnboundLocalError: local variable 'units' referenced before assignment\n```\n\nThis makes it impossible to generate SVG QR codes using the library."
